WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:06.880
How can we overtake smoothly and save
energy? A car is passing in the right-hand
lane.

2
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.880
A button sets the overtaking goal. The
instruction expresses smoothness and energy
preferences for local-model interpretation.

3
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:23.880
Both candidates overtake. A predicts a
26-second finish with higher energy; B
predicts a 29-second finish, allowing more
time.

4
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.880
After comparison, B better matches the
preferences.

5
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:34.880
A different offer is accepted: a 26-second
finish and a 4.5-second lane transition.

6
00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:40.880
Both evaluations inform a new plan: a
29-second finish and 4.5-second
transitions.

7
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.880
The goal is retained. Ego enters the
right-hand lane.

8
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.880
Ego moves forward and gradually passes the
slow lead car.

9
00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.880
Ego returns to the original lane. The solid
line shows recorded execution.

10
00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:59.880
Simulation complete. Recorded complete-task
model energy is about 57 watt-hours.
